{"title":"Career Roadmap · Paediatric Therapist","role":"Paediatric Therapist","summary":"A Paediatric Therapist supports children and adolescents who have developmental, neurological, musculoskeletal, motor, functional or mobility-related difficulties.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences","Course":"Physiotherapy – Sports / Neuro / Paediatric Rehabilitation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Paediatric Therapist supports children and adolescents who have developmental, neurological, musculoskeletal, motor, functional or mobility-related difficulties."},{"type":"p","text":"For a physiotherapy-oriented pathway, the professional may work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gross-motor development"},{"text":"Balance and coordination"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Strength and endurance"},{"text":"Posture"},{"text":"Gait"},{"text":"Functional independence"},{"text":"Developmental rehabilitation"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation"},{"text":"Sports-related rehabilitation for children"},{"text":"Family/caregiver education"},{"text":"Assistive-device use and functional training"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Common settings include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Paediatric hospitals"},{"text":"Rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Child-development centres"},{"text":"Special schools"},{"text":"Early-intervention centres"},{"text":"Multispecialty hospitals"},{"text":"Paediatric clinics"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation programs"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Paediatric Therapist” is a broad term. Physiotherapy, occupational therapy, speech-language therapy and other rehabilitation professions have different scopes. A student following a physiotherapy pathway should practice within the scope of physiotherapy and applicable professional registration/licensing requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build strong foundations in anatomy, physiology, kinesiology, exercise therapy and paediatric development"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work as a physiotherapy professional in paediatric rehabilitation and develop clinical experience"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Specialize in paediatric neurorehabilitation, developmental rehabilitation, gait or early intervention"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward senior clinical, rehabilitation-team leadership, research, education or specialized paediatric rehabilitation roles"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Learning Plan","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Biomedical Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Human development"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Communication skills"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong understanding of:"},{"type":"p","text":"Musculoskeletal System"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Nervous System"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Cardiorespiratory System"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Child Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Physiotherapy Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biomechanics"},{"text":"Kinesiology"},{"text":"Exercise therapy"},{"text":"Electrotherapy"},{"text":"Therapeutic exercise"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal conditions"},{"text":"Neurology"},{"text":"Orthopaedics"},{"text":"Clinical assessment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Begin connecting:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Movement","Motor Control","Function","Participation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Paediatric Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental milestones"},{"text":"Paediatric neurology"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Developmental coordination difficulties"},{"text":"Muscular disorders"},{"text":"Spina bifida"},{"text":"Developmental delay"},{"text":"Paediatric orthopaedic conditions"},{"text":"Gait abnormalities"},{"text":"Balance problems"},{"text":"Motor-control disorders"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how rehabilitation goals differ according to:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Age","Development","Diagnosis","Functional Ability","Family Environment"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Final Year — Clinical Specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain supervised clinical exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Paediatric physiotherapy"},{"text":"Neurorehabilitation"},{"text":"Early intervention"},{"text":"Developmental rehabilitation"},{"text":"Paediatric orthopaedics"},{"text":"Gait training"},{"text":"Balance training"},{"text":"Functional mobility"},{"text":"Assistive devices"},{"text":"Family/caregiver education"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The focus should be on individualized, developmentally appropriate and function-oriented rehabilitation."}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"A. Child Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gross-motor milestones"},{"text":"Fine-motor development"},{"text":"Postural development"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Gait development"},{"text":"Functional independence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"B. Paediatric Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to assess, under appropriate supervision:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Posture"},{"text":"Muscle strength"},{"text":"Range of motion"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Motor control"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Gait"},{"text":"Functional abilities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"C. Therapeutic Exercise"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand age-appropriate approaches to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strengthening"},{"text":"Stretching"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Motor control"},{"text":"Endurance"},{"text":"Functional movement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"D. Neurorehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Neuromuscular disorders"},{"text":"Developmental delay"},{"text":"Spina bifida"},{"text":"Paediatric stroke/neurological conditions"},{"text":"Motor-control difficulties"}]},{"type":"h","text":"E. Family-Centred Care"},{"type":"p","text":"A paediatric therapist works not only with the child but also with:"},{"type":"p","text":"Child"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Parents/Caregivers"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Teachers"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Physiotherapist"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Occupational Therapist"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Speech Therapist"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Paediatrician"}]},{"heading":"Practical Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Developmental Milestone Tracker"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an educational dashboard covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Age"},{"text":"Gross-motor milestones"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Functional skills"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"h","text":"Excel → Power BI"},{"type":"p","text":"This should be used for educational tracking, not independent diagnosis."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Paediatric Rehabilitation Progress Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Track objective rehabilitation measures such as:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Baseline","Functional Assessment","Rehabilitation Plan","Periodic Assessment","Progress Tracking","Goal Review"]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible metrics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Walking ability"},{"text":"Balance measures"},{"text":"Range of motion"},{"text":"Functional mobility"},{"text":"Exercise tolerance"},{"text":"Goal completion"}]},{"type":"h","text":